<SiteLayout title="About — Why This Anime Site Exists | AnimeSparks" socialTitle="About — Why This Anime Site Exists" description="AnimeSparks explores anime through deeper analysis, honest opinions, and storytelling breakdowns for viewers who want more than hype." canonical={`${SITE}/about`} image={homeImage}>
  <main class="about-page"><header class="shell about-hero"><div><p class="kicker lime">Personal Blog</p><h1>Behind <br /><span class="red">The Sparks</span></h1><p>AnimeSparks is written by one person. No ghostwriters. No filler. Just real watch time turned into reviews, lists, and deep dives.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="read-button" href="#writer">Meet the writer ↗</a><a class="outline-button" href="/blogs">Read the blog ↗</a></div></div><img src="/me.jpeg" alt="AnimeSparks author" /></header><div class="about-marquee">/// MISSION START /// DECODING CULTURE /// NO FILLER /// HONEST TAKES ///</div><section class="shell about-section"><div><p class="kicker red">The mission</p><h2>Our Manifesto<span class="red">.</span></h2><p>01. Anime isn’t a genre. It’s a medium. I write to decode the craft, the themes, and the choices hiding inside every frame.</p><p>02. This site is supposed to feel alive. Loud typography, sharp borders, and a little chaos to match the medium.</p><p>03. No corporate tone. No fake hype. If it’s mid, I’ll say it. If it’s peak, I’ll say that too.</p><div class="button-row"><a class="read-button" href="/blogs">Read articles ↗</a><a class="outline-button" href="/categories">Browse categories ↗</a></div></div><div class="about-visual">SOLO<br />OPS</div></section><section class="about-values"><div class="shell"><h2>Core <span class="red">Values</span></h2><div class="value-grid"><article><h3>Visual Obsession</h3><p>I pay attention to composition, animation choices, and the stuff most recaps ignore.</p></article><article><h3>Story First</h3><p>Themes, writing, character logic. I care about what the story is doing, not just what it looks like.</p></article><article><h3>Honesty</h3><p>No forced positivity. If something falls apart, I’ll call it out and explain why.</p></article></div></div></section><section id="writer" class="shell about-section"><img src="/me.jpeg" alt="The AnimeSparks writer" loading="lazy" /><div><p class="kicker red">Solo author</p><h2>Meet The Writer<span class="red">.</span></h2><p>I started AnimeSparks to write the kind of anime articles I wanted to read: clean, sharp, and obsessed with detail. No fluff intros. No “10/10 peak” spam. Just real thoughts, explained properly.</p><h3>What You’ll Get Here</h3><ul><li>Reviews that explain the “why”, not just a score.</li><li>Deep dives into themes and character writing.</li><li>Lists that feel curated, not copy-pasted.</li></ul><a class="read-button" href="/blogs">Read my latest ↗</a></div></section><section class="shell about-cta"><h2>Join the conversation<span class="red">.</span></h2><p>Have a story tip, correction, or a series worth discussing?</p><a class="read-button" href="/contact">Contact AnimeSparks ↗</a></section></main>
